WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.371
The answer to check five: the
tag's addresses are shared by

2
00:00:03.371 --> 00:00:06.975
every Front Door customer, so the
header has to prove it's yours.

3
00:00:06.975 --> 00:00:08.663
Scene six, what leaves.

4
00:00:08.663 --> 00:00:13.674
Microsoft Learn's Zero Trust recommendations
for Azure Firewall check that outbound

5
00:00:13.674 --> 00:00:15.831
traffic routes through the firewall,

6
00:00:15.831 --> 00:00:19.799
with threat intelligence and
intrusion detection in alert and deny.

7
00:00:19.799 --> 00:00:24.087
The portal's web subnet sends its
default route straight to the internet.

8
00:00:24.087 --> 00:00:28.124
Its jump subnet sends it to an
appliance that isn't the hub firewall.

9
00:00:28.124 --> 00:00:30.450
And the hub policy is still in alert.

10
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:35.286
The kit writes Learn's draft-and-deploy
commands for the move to deny into a plan,

11
00:00:35.286 --> 00:00:39.890
which it never runs, because deploying
replaces the whole applied policy.
